[5.358701, "o", "\u001b[33m      \"FDIR isolates at most one wheel so dual derates leave a bad wheel active. Friction pair 2/3\r\n      looks resilient, 0/1 untested. Battery thinnest for heater plus friction at beta~0. Partial\r\n      and staggered onsets evade isolation. Probe boundaries and novel no-RW, partial, staggered\r\n      cases.\"\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[2m(ground truth, never shown to it: fdir isolates at most one wheel, min_avail = 3)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m== 4. Recorded gated-repair calls (roles: diagnosis, patch proposal) + gate decisions ==\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[5.361709, "o", "  \u001b[1mr1t1\u001b[0m model muse-spark-1.3 latency 56s request id: not logged; first committed 2026-11-03T23:13:09-05:00 (commit 82058c1)\r\n"]
[5.362161, "o", "    diagnosis:\r\n\u001b[33m      FDIR allows only one isolation and latches the first wheel to exceed residual threshold. Mild\r\n      friction severity 0.2 gives ~0.45 mNm residual just above 0.3 mNm threshold and often trips\r\n      first. A later more severe friction/derate then cannot be isolated, leaving the worse wheel in\r\n      the active set while the healthier wheel sits isolated, reducing controllability and causing\r\n      attitude-loss/saturation that no-FDIR avoids.\u001b[0m\r\n    patch proposed: {\"isolation_swap\": true, \"swap_ratio\": 2.0}\r\n    gate: \u001b[31mreject\u001b[0m - rejected: 20 new violations in 20 runs (20 previously clean) (evaluation stopped early after 861 runs)\r\n"]
[5.364379, "o", "  \u001b[1mr1t2\u001b[0m model muse-spark-1.3 latency 83s request id: not logged; first committed 2026-11-03T23:13:09-05:00 (commit 82058c1)\r\n    patch proposed: {\"fdir_abs_Nm\": 0.0006}\r\n"]
